<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bückeburg Palace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buckeburg">Bückeburg</a> Palace is the residence of the princes of Schaumburg-Lippe in Bückeburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, developed from a 14th-century moated castle and rebuilt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> style around 1600 by Count Ernest of Holstein-Schaumburg. Its chapel and golden hall are notable works of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser-renaissance">Weser Renaissance</a>, and it remains the home of the princely family.</p></div>
